110897617001-695ce124-ce0d-42e9-8250-b3b42f534218"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-311_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"3d705fec-b472-45ca-b9ca-e9472648a082","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Starting (session 3d705fec): file impact set to the new module tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_fix_versions_live.py and the suite README; running plan review on the Anthropic API.","timestamp":1794517976740683001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Commit 6b431564084 (tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_fix_versions_live.py + README section): make verify exit 0, 15:03-15:43 PST 2026-11-12 (21221 passed, 29 skipped; integration 218 passed, 2 skipped). The 4 tests collect under pytest -m external tests/external/live_jira_dc with the jira_live marker. A local run against Docker DC was not possible: under arm64 emulation the harness Tomcat did not start within the plugin's 1-hour limit (BUILD FAILURE), so the live evidence will come from the jira-dc-harness job after merge. Search waits were added before each follow-up pass, because the outbound diff reads fixVersions from JQL search and would otherwise re-plan an add that already landed. Pushed as Gerrit 3384.","timestamp":1794527110897617001}],"created_at":1794513974422110663,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"316bd268-195f-4748-8fa7-1fd65924a0dc","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"21ec-3e9b-4a27-4775"},{"link_uuid":"dbb03a87-cb82-4c01-af04-681b6fd6d58b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7f23-e3dc-a2a6-457b"}],"description":"## Problem\n\nFix-version sync (ADR 0124, epic `inferior-seaborgium-aruanas`) is tested only against fakes. Unit tests cover the diffs, the transport writes and the release alerts. The one integration test, `tests/integration/reconciler/test_reconcile_releases_roundtrip.py`, runs real `reconcile_once` passes over an in-memory Jira fake. Production was checked live once, against Jira Cloud (`plucky-jetblack-parrot`, `cognitive-sooty-angelfish`).\n\nThe Jira DC suite in `tests/external/live_jira_dc` has no fix-version test. That suite runs a real Jira DC server in Docker, in the `jira-dc-harness` job of `.github/workflows/external-integration.yml`. The DC write path (`src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py`) and the DC version read have never run against a real server.\n\n## Plan\n\nAdd a fix-version scenario module to `tests/external/live_jira_dc`. Reuse that suite's existing fixtures: the harness project, the bridge configuration and the reconcile runner. Follow the patterns in `test_multi_project_rehearsal.py` and `test_transport.py`. The scenario runs real reconcile passes against the Docker DC server and covers:\n\n1. Inbound sync: a version created in the DC project through the REST API and set on an issue's `fixVersions` appears in the bound rebar ticket's `releases`.\n2. Outbound add: a release added in rebar for a version the project has is written to the issue's `fixVersions`. Adding a second release also writes it and keeps the first, so the write is per item.\n3. Outbound remove: a release removed in rebar disappears from `fixVersions`, and the other entries stay.\n4. A missing version is held back: a release naming a version the DC project lacks is not written. Instead the ticket gets a BRIDGE_ALERT, and the alert clears once that version is created and a later pass writes it.\n\nThe test must leave the harness project clean, with no leftover versions or issues that would affect other tests in the module order.\n\n## Implementation notes (added 2026-11-12 after plan review)\n\n- **Per item, shown from the pass itself.** Jira's end state cannot tell a per-item `update` from a whole-list `fields` replace, because rebar holds the full intended set. The pass logs `RECON: outbound_update key=<KEY> changed=[<whole fields>] ... releases=<n>` (`outbound_mutation_builders.py`), where `releases` counts per-item add/remove mutations. Scenarios 2 and 3 assert that the pass adding the second release, and the pass removing one, log `releases=1` for that key with `fixVersions` absent from `changed`. A whole-list write would show `fixVersions` in `changed` or a count of 2.\n- **Intent.** Outbound add and remove only act on releases rebar itself set (the ever-seen intent set in `local_label_intent.py`). Scenarios 2 to 4 set releases with `rebar.edit_ticket(..., add_releases=/remove_releases=)`, never through inbound, so they exercise that path.\n- **Versions and cleanup.** Versions are created and deleted through DC REST as admin (`POST /rest/api/2/version`, `DELETE /rest/api/2/version/{id}`), each with a unique `rbj-<label>-<hex>` name, deleted in `finally`. Each test uses its own `jira_dc_project`, whose teardown deletes the project as a backstop.\n- **README.** `tests/external/live_jira_dc/README.md` has no scenario list today; the change adds a short \"Fix-version scenarios\" section naming the module and its 4 scenarios.\n- **Module:** `tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_fix_versions_live.py`, reusing `bound_dc_issue`, `dc_store_copy_repo`, `dc_transport`, `dc_request`, `jira_dc_project` and scoped `bootstrap-strict` passes.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A new test module under `tests/external/live_jira_dc/` covers scenarios 1 to 4 above against the Docker DC server, with real reconcile passes and no fakes on the Jira side.\n- [ ] Every new test carries the `external` marker. The new tests are picked up by `pytest -m external tests/external/live_jira_dc`, the command the `jira-dc-harness` job runs.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] A `jira-dc-harness` run of `external-integration.yml` on a commit containing the new module passes, with the new tests listed as passed. The run URL is recorded in a comment on this ticket.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes on the change.\n- [ ] `tests/external/live_jira_dc/README.md` lists the new scenario.\n- [ ] Scenarios 2 and 3 show per-item writes from the pass's own `RECON: outbound_update` line (`releases=1`, no `fixVersions` in `changed`).\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_fix_versions_live.py","reason":"new fix-version scenario module (scenarios 1-4) against the Docker DC server"},{"path":"tests/external/live_jira_dc/README.md","reason":"list the new scenario"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","7f23-e3dc-a2a6-457b"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"35434bdd-c31a-4f0a-9507-63ead204dcdb","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"af08-19c2-87b4-41d3","ticket_type":"story","title":"Live-test fix-version sync in the Jira DC Docker suite","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["37735220-f256-41ca-9669-afdeb6be1df8","316bd268-195f-4748-8fa7-1fd65924a0dc","dbb03a87-cb82-4c01-af04-681b6fd6d58b","eb503315-af0f-4caa-bbb1-307ee34c4745","0574006f-cb7f-4a6e-9356-72affeccfa6d","1ccf21eb-2a8d-4709-b836-729e8685dc16","e0d0434d-9c01-48d1-b1ff-00ea991330f9","35434bdd-c31a-4f0a-9507-63ead204dcdb","eb6d8d35-8492-447b-baaf-2a9465516332","695ce124-ce0d-42e9-8250-b3b42f534218"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794527110897617002,"uuid":"fee514ce-86b7-4c9c-af4b-4286bb3b6e2b"}